---
source: crates/notifications/src/lib.rs
expression: email.body
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <style>
        body { margin: 0; padding: 0; font-family: Ubuntu, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; }
        .email-container { max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; }
        .email-content { padding: 20px; }
        .logo { text-align: center; padding: 20px 0; }
        .divider { border-top: 1px dashed grey; margin: 20px 0; }
        .dear-line { font-size: 20px; color: #512d0b; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px; }
        .body-text { font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.4; margin-bottom: 10px; }
        .signature { font-size: 14px; color: #000000; margin-top: 15px; }
        .identifier { background-color: #dadada; padding: 2px 3px; border-radius: 2px; font-family: monospace; font-weight: bold; }
        a { color: #5072EB; text-decoration: none; }
        .button {
            display: inline-block;
            background-color: #5072EB;
            color: white;
            padding: 12px 24px;
            border-radius: 4px;
            text-decoration: none;
            margin: 25px 0 0 0;
            font-weight: 400;
            font-size: 17px;
        }
        ul { margin: 10px 0; padding-left: 20px; }
        li { margin: 5px 0; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="email-container">
        <div class="logo">
            <img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/estuary-marketing-strapi-uploads/uploads//estuary_logo_comfy_14513ca434/estuary_logo_comfy_14513ca434.jpg" alt="Estuary Logo" style="max-width: 200px;">
        </div>
        <div class="divider"></div>
        <div class="email-content">
            <p class="body-text">
                Bindings of your Estuary materialization <span class="identifier">acmeCo/test/materialization</span> have been automatically disabled. Disabled bindings don't update their destination resources.
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Collection <span class="identifier">acmeCo/test/orders</span>, resource <span class="identifier">public.orders</span>:
                    <div style="background-color: #f4f4f4; color: #000000; border-left: 3px solid #dadada; margin: 8px 0 16px; padding: 12px;">
                        <strong>Disabled because of an incompatible schema change</strong>
                        <pre style="font-family: monospace; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 8px 0 0; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; word-break: break-word;">group-by key changed from [&quot;id&quot;] to [&quot;order_id&quot;]</pre>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    Collection <span class="identifier">acmeCo/test/customers</span>, resource <span class="identifier">customers</span>:
                    <div style="background-color: #f4f4f4; color: #000000; border-left: 3px solid #dadada; margin: 8px 0 16px; padding: 12px;">
                        <strong>Disabled because of an incompatible schema change</strong>
                        <pre style="font-family: monospace; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 8px 0 0; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; word-break: break-word;">conflict for field &quot;amount&quot;: field is within the desired depth but connector cannot support this field without a backfill (field type changed)</pre>
                    </div>
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="body-text">
                We try our best to handle schema changes automatically. In this case(s), we weren't able to. In order to restore a disabled binding, you must backfill it.
            </p>
            <p class="body-text">
                Beware that if the collection being materialized is stored in Estuary's trial storage bucket, data older than 20 days is not available. You can either proceed with that limitation and backfill the materialization binding, or you can re-backfill from the source by performing a dataflow reset, which will re-capture all of the data from the source.
            </p>
            <p class="body-text">
                If you need help, you can <a href="http://dashboard.estuary.test/materializations/details/overview?catalogName=acmeCo/test/materialization" target="_blank" rel="noopener">view the task status and bindings</a>, reach out to our team via <a href="https://go.estuary.dev/slack">Slack</a> (#support), or reply to this email.
            </p>            <div class="signature">
                Thanks,<br>
                Estuary Team
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
